.Dd November 18, 2026
.Dt PI4-XHCI 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm pi4-xhci
.Nd Raspberry Pi 4 VL805 xHCI boot-keyboard driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar bar Ns = Ns Ar n
.Op Ar bar_size Ns = Ns Ar bytes
.Op Ar dma Ns = Ns Ar bytes
.Op Ar irq Ns = Ns Ar line
.Op Ar test
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
drives the Pi 4 VL805 USB 3 host function through the first-party xHCI
controller and the USB-core boot-keyboard path.
In the board mode the launcher passes the BAR, configuration page, DMA and
legacy IRQ handles in that order.
The driver reads the vendor and device IDs, maps BAR0, starts the controller,
resets the root port, addresses the device, selects the HID boot protocol and
decodes boot reports.
Decoded ASCII bytes are pushed to the
.Dq kbd:
queue served by
.Nm usb-hid ;
a missing queue is not a driver failure.
.Pp
With
.Ar test
the driver uses the synthetic D1 ring and a synthetic boot keyboard.
No PCI or MMIO resource is touched on that path.
The
.Ar pi4-usb
qtest exercises it.
.Pp
The VL805 BAR size, IRQ routing and real board enumeration are UNVERIFIED
until the UI1 board run.
A missing controller, keyboard or resource must fail without blocking the UART
console.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d/usb-xhci.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/usb-xhci.toml
Optional one-shot boot probe service.
.It Pa /etc/drivers.toml
PCI entry for vendor 0x1106 and device 0x3483.
.El
